{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nNow I have all the information I need. Let me analyze and create the plan:\n\n**Analysis of the inputs:**\n\n1. **Release notes (RN-101 to RN-104):\n- RN-101: Audit translator schema drift before removing legacy parser shim\n- RN-102: Backfill dependency-graph fixtures for plan contract\n- RN-103: Enable dashboard summary behind kill switch after schema stable\n- RN-104: Update runbook after summary path proven in canary\n\n2. **Dependencies identified:**\n- Dashboard summary depends on step-id schema from translator\n- Dashboard must not ship until dependency-graph fixtures reflect new schema\n- Runbook only stabilizes after rollout/rollback shape are known\n\n3. **Test evidence:**\n- `tests/plan_contract.py` fails when new step ids introduced without fixture updates\n- Canary coverage exists for dashboard but not for bad dependency ordering\n\n4. **Repo state:\n- Legacy parser shim masks schema drift\n- Dashboard is user-visible and renders whatever order translator emits\n\n**Logical ordering:**\n1. First: RN-101 (audit schema drift) - bounded, reduces ambiguity\n2. Second: RN-102 (backfill fixtures) - required before dashboard can work\n3. Third: RN-103 (enable dashboard) - depends on schema + fixtures\n4. Fourth: RN-104 (update runbook) - depends on rollout being proven\n\nLet me create the brief:\n\n"}}
